  "lineage": "Burmese mahagita (\"great song\") classical Burmese art-music canon, comprising the codified repertoire of the late-Konbaung-dynasty (eighteenth-nineteenth century) royal court at Mandalay. The mahagita corpus is organized through several song-categories (kyò devotional-style, bwèh ceremonial-style, thachingan classical-song-form, etc.) with distinct modal-and-rhythmic conventions per category. Performance configuration ranges from solo voice with saung gauk arched-harp accompaniment (the most refined chamber form) to fuller ensembles with pat-tala xylophone, hsaing-waing drum-circle, and additional wind-instruments. The post-1885 British annexation of Burma terminated the royal-court patronage; the post-1962 Burma Socialist Programme cultural-policy and the State School of Music and Drama anchor modern transmission.",
